     46          /* General Notes: Define one device to compile options for that device. */
     47          /* Will not compile correctly if no device is defined.  Not all options */
     48          /* for each device are supported.  There is no error checking for data  */
     49          /* entry.  Defines may not remove all code that is not relevant to the  */
     50          /* device. This example was written for an 8051-type micro, the DS2250/ */
     51          /* DS5000.  The program must be modified to work properly on typical    */
     52          /* 8051 variants (i.e. assign I2C bus to unused port pins).  This       */
     53          /* program is for example only and is not supported by Dallas Maxim     */
